{# ===========================================================================
   WINNER HEALTH — the chart room for extended US winners  (TOP ANATOMY W1)
   winner_health.html.j2  →  site/winner_health.html

   Data: one nightly context dict `wh` (schema winner_health.v1) passed by
   scripts/build_winner_health_page.py. Everything renders server-side; the page
   ships NO fetch, NO chart library and NO page JS beyond the shared chrome.

   Design contract: research/top_anatomy/W1_SURFACE_DESIGN_SPEC.md (visual LAW)
   + docs/DESIGN_DOCTRINE.md (content law — wins on conflict).
   Program: research/TOP_ANATOMY_MASTERPLAN_BY_FABLE.md §5-W1 (display gate).

   Foundations (non-negotiable — spec §2):
   - DISPLAY TIER, zero authority. No rank, no score, no gate, no sizing, no
     composite. States are GROUPS; inside a group the order is trailing gain,
     a fact, not a ranking. Nothing here is a buy, sell, trim or exit rule.
   - Colour comes from theme.css tokens. The page-local MATURATION RAMP
     (--m1..--m4) layers OVER them and never redefines a token. The ramp is
     NON-directional on purpose (maturation is wear, not price direction), so
     it must NOT flip under 红涨绿跌. Anything that IS directional (gains,
     drops) routes through --ink-up / --ink-down so ZH flips it automatically.
   - The dark plane lives on :root (NEVER html[data-theme="dark"] — a first
     visit carries no data-theme attribute at all and that rule would match
     nothing). Light overrides on html[data-theme="light"].
   - Tier 1 = state + plain-word stance under hard word budgets. Every number
     has a plain-word neighbour. Mechanics, n's, windows and provenance live in
     LENS hovers (Tier 2). No study names, no state enums, no bare statistics.
   - Falsifier / refutation vocabulary and earned-authority language never appear.
   =========================================================================== #}
{# house pattern (china / hk / canada): plain import at the top, lens_css() once in
   the body. `with context` is deliberately NOT used — the partial needs none. #}
{% import "_lens.html.j2" as lens %}
{% macro t(en, zh='') -%}
<span class="l-en">{{ en }}</span><span class="l-zh">{{ zh if zh else en }}</span>
{%- endmacro %}

{# ── signed percent, typographic minus. Figures only, never words. ── #}
{% macro pc(x, dp=0) -%}
{%- if x is not defined or x is none -%}—{%- else -%}
{{ (('%+.' ~ dp ~ 'f') % (x * 100)) | replace('-', '−') }}%
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}

{# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   THE SIGNATURE — the high-water rule.
   Every spark is measured against the run's OWN highest close: a dashed rule
   at that level, the price line in neutral ink, and a state-tinted UNDERWATER
   area filling everything between the rule and the price from the session the
   high was set. On a name still at its high the area is a sliver you cannot
   see; on one that has changed character it is the loudest thing in the row.
   Same picture, four readings — the page's whole thesis at 104×30.
   Price ink is deliberately NEUTRAL: direction is communicated by the gain
   figure beside it (--ink-up/--ink-down, which the ZH swap flips), so the
   spark never carries two colour systems at once.
   Static by contract (docs/ILLUSTRATIONS.md): settled data never pulses.
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
{% macro spark(vals, hi, w=104, h=30) -%}
{%- set pts = (vals | reject('none') | list) if vals else [] -%}
{%- if pts | length > 2 -%}
  {%- set n = pts | length -%}
  {%- set win_max = pts | max -%}
  {%- set top = [win_max, (hi if hi is not none else win_max)] | max -%}
  {%- set bot = pts | min -%}
  {%- set rng = (top - bot) if (top - bot) > 0.000001 else 1 -%}
  {%- set pad = 4 -%}
  {%- set span = h - (2 * pad) -%}
  {%- set y_hi = pad -%}
  {%- set y_last = (pad + ((top - pts[-1]) / rng) * span) | round(2) -%}
  {#- The underwater region starts the session the high was SET, not at the left
      edge: before that the name simply had not got there yet, and shading the
      run-up would make every extended name look equally worn. When the run's
      high predates this window, the whole window is under it — which is itself
      the reading, so the fill correctly starts at 0. -#}
  {%- set hi_i = pts.index(win_max) if (top - win_max) < 0.000001 else 0 -%}
  <svg class="sp" viewBox="0 0 {{ w }} {{ h }}" preserveAspectRatio="none" role="img" aria-hidden="true">
    {#- the underwater area: everything between the run's own high-water rule and
        the price. Not a magnitude bar — it is the SHAPE of how long, and how
        far, this name has been trading under its own best close. The number
        itself is stated in words in the row beside it. -#}
    {%- if hi_i < (n - 1) %}
    <path class="sp-uw" d="M{{ (hi_i / (n - 1) * w) | round(2) }},{{ y_hi }}
      {%- for i in range(hi_i, n) %} L{{ (i / (n - 1) * w) | round(2) }},{{ (pad + ((top - pts[i]) / rng) * span) | round(2) }}{% endfor %} L{{ w }},{{ y_hi }} Z"/>
    {%- endif %}
    <line class="sp-hw" x1="0" y1="{{ y_hi }}" x2="{{ w }}" y2="{{ y_hi }}" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"/>
    <polyline class="sp-ln" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke" points="
      {%- for i in range(n) %}{{ (i / (n - 1) * w) | round(2) }},{{ (pad + ((top - pts[i]) / rng) * span) | round(2) }} {% endfor -%}"/>
    <circle class="sp-dot" cx="{{ w }}" cy="{{ y_last }}" r="2.1"/>
  </svg>
{%- else -%}
  <span class="sp-null">{{ t('no history', '暂无历史') }}</span>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}

{# ── wear marks: 0-3 filled slots = how many things have slipped. A non-verbal
      count that scans across 100 rows; the words sit right beside it, so this
      is decoration for the screen reader and is hidden from it. ── #}
{# The class is built INSIDE the attribute on purpose: emitting ` class="on"`
   as an interpolated string ships &#34;on&#34; under autoescape, so the mark
   silently never fills. #}
{% macro wear(k) -%}
<span class="wear" aria-hidden="true">{% for i in range(3) %}<i class="{{ 'on' if i < k else 'off' }}"></i>{% endfor %}</span>
{%- endmacro %}

{# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   ANALOG MEMORY — "in the library".
   A LENS record card: what runs shaped like this one went on to do. Framed as
   lived history with an honest episode-level N and a named track, never as a
   forecast. Below the honest-N floor the card SAYS the library is too thin
   rather than printing a rate nobody should read.
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
{% macro analog(a, lib, M) -%}
{%- if a and a.n -%}
{%- set thin = (a.n < 12) -%}
<span class="lens-term lib" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Similar past runs in the library">
  <span class="l-en">{{ a.n }} like this</span><span class="l-zh">{{ a.n }} 例相似</span>
  <span class="lens-src" data-lens-kind="record" hidden>
    <div class="lens-hd">
      <span class="lens-ill"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 5.5h5.5a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v11a1.6 1.6 0 0 0-1.6-1.6H4Z"/><path d="M20 5.5h-5.5a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v11a1.6 1.6 0 0 1 1.6-1.6H20Z"/></svg></span>
      <span class="lens-hgroup">
        <span class="lens-kick">{{ t('In the library', '历史资料库') }}</span>
        <span class="lens-title">{{ t(a.n ~ ' past runs shaped like this', '资料库中 ' ~ a.n ~ ' 段形态相似的行情') }}</span>
      </span>
    </div>
    {%- if thin %}
    <div class="lens-body">{{ t('Only ' ~ a.n ~ ' past runs match this one closely enough to count — too few to read as a pattern. The count is shown so you know how thin the record is, not so you can lean on it.',
                                '与本次行情足够相似的历史样本只有 ' ~ a.n ~ ' 段 —— 太少，不足以当作规律来看。这里把次数写出来，是为了让你知道记录有多薄，而不是让你据此下判断。') }}
      {%- if a.track != 'W' %} {{ t('It also draws only on names with long price history, so runs that ended in a delisting are under-represented.',
                                    '而且它只取有长期价格历史的个股，因此以退市收场的行情在样本中偏少。') }}{% endif %}</div>
    {%- else %}
    <div class="lensx-rows">
      <div class="lensx-row warn">
        <span class="lensx-k">{{ t('Fell back hard', '大幅回落') }}</span>
        <span class="lensx-v"><span class="l-en"><b>{{ a.topped_63td }} of {{ a.n }}</b> dropped {{ lib.drawdown_pct | default(20) }}% or more from their high within three months{% if a.topped_63td %} — about 1 in {{ ((a.n / a.topped_63td) | round | int) if a.topped_63td else '—' }}{% endif %}.</span><span class="l-zh"><b>{{ a.n }} 段里有 {{ a.topped_63td }} 段</b>在三个月内从高点回落 {{ lib.drawdown_pct | default(20) }}% 或更多{% if a.topped_63td %} —— 大约每 {{ ((a.n / a.topped_63td) | round | int) if a.topped_63td else '—' }} 段有 1 段{% endif %}。</span></span>
      </div>
      <div class="lensx-row up">
        <span class="lensx-k">{{ t('Kept going', '继续上行') }}</span>
        <span class="lensx-v"><span class="l-en">The other <b>{{ a.n - a.topped_63td }}</b> carried on{% if a.median_further_gain is not none %} — a typical further gain of <b>{{ pc(a.median_further_gain) }}</b>{% endif %}.</span><span class="l-zh">其余 <b>{{ a.n - a.topped_63td }}</b> 段继续上行{% if a.median_further_gain is not none %}，典型的后续涨幅为 <b>{{ pc(a.median_further_gain) }}</b>{% endif %}。</span></span>
      </div>
      {%- if a.median_drop_from_high is not none %}
      <div class="lensx-row dn">
        <span class="lensx-k">{{ t('When they fell', '回落时') }}</span>
        <span class="lensx-v"><span class="l-en">The typical drop from the high was <b>{{ pc(a.median_drop_from_high) }}</b>.</span><span class="l-zh">从高点回落的典型幅度是 <b>{{ pc(a.median_drop_from_high) }}</b>。</span></span>
      </div>
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
    {#- The survivorship disclosure (G0.2) lives HERE, in wrapping prose, not in
        the receipt: receipt items are nowrap tokens and a sentence-length value
        is silently clipped there. -#}
    <div class="lensx-note">{{ t('This is what those runs did — history, not a forecast. Runs are matched on shape and age, never on the company or its industry.',
                                 '这是那些行情当年走过的路 —— 是历史，不是预测。匹配只看走势形态和运行时长，与公司本身或所属行业无关。') }}
      {#- The per-tier disclosure is PROSE and lives here, never in the receipt:
          `.lens-receipt .r-i` is nowrap, so a sentence-length value is silently
          clipped there (W1 §9.3). -#}
      {%- if M %} {{ t('Matched only against past runs that also cleared this group\'s bar.',
                       '只与同样达到本组门槛的历史行情做匹配。') }}{% endif %}
      {%- if a.track == 'W' %} {{ t('The record includes names that later delisted.', '这份记录包含了后来退市的个股。') }}
      {%- else %} {{ t('It draws only on names with long price history, so runs that ended in a delisting are under-represented.',
                       '它只取有长期价格历史的个股，因此以退市收场的行情在样本中偏少。') }}{% endif %}</div>
    {%- endif %}
    <div class="lens-receipt">
      <span class="r-i"><span class="r-k">N</span>{{ a.n }} {{ t('episodes', '段行情') }}</span>
      {%- if lib.window_start and lib.window_end %}<span class="r-i"><span class="r-k">{{ t('Window', '区间') }}</span>{{ lib.window_start }} → {{ lib.window_end }}</span>{% endif %}
      <span class="r-i"><span class="r-k">{{ t('Names', '样本') }}</span>{% if a.track == 'W' %}{{ t('whole US market', '全市场') }}{% else %}{{ t('curated', '精选池') }}{% endif %}</span>
    </div>
  </span>
</span>
{%- else -%}
<span class="lib-null" data-tip-en="No past run in this group's library is close enough in shape and age to show a count." data-tip-zh="本分组的资料库里，没有在形态和运行时长上足够接近的历史行情，因此不显示次数。">{{ t('no match', '无相似样本') }}</span>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}

{# ── the per-tier row figure. Three tiers, three measures, one cell.
      `atr_x` is a DISTANCE, not a direction — it is >= the bar by construction,
      so directional ink would print a permanent green (permanent red in ZH) that
      means nothing. Neutral ink, tabular figures, one decimal. ── #}
{% macro figcell(r, T) -%}
{%- set fg = T.figure | default('r126') -%}
{%- if fg == 'atr_x' -%}
  {%- if r.atr_x is defined and r.atr_x is not none -%}
  <span class="fig neutral">{{ '%.1f' % r.atr_x }}×</span>
  {%- else -%}<span class="fig neutral">—</span>{%- endif -%}
{%- elif fg == 'r63' -%}
  <span class="fig{{ ' dn' if (r.r63 is defined and r.r63 is not none and r.r63 < 0) else '' }}">{{ pc(r.r63) }}</span>
{%- else -%}
  <span class="fig{{ ' dn' if (r.r126 is defined and r.r126 is not none and r.r126 < 0) else '' }}">{{ pc(r.r126) }}</span>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}

{# ── PROVENANCE, appended to every leg hover (§4.6b). The mandate requires each
      receipt to name its own tier's library — and, just as importantly, to say
      which legs are cut from NO library at all, so a reader never has to assume
      that three fixed rules were re-fitted per group. The engine stamps the
      class (`cut`); the tier NAME is display copy and lives here. ── #}
{% macro prov_en(g, M) -%}
{%- if g.cut == 'fixed' %} This is a fixed rule, the same in every group.
{%- else %} Cut from past runs in {{ M.en }} only — never from another group's history.{% endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}
{% macro prov_zh(g, M) -%}
{%- if g.cut == 'fixed' %} 这是一条固定规则，各分组通用。
{%- else %} 这一标准只取自「{{ M.zh }}」分组内的历史行情 —— 不使用其他分组的历史。{% endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}

{# ── one name row ── #}
{% macro namerow(r, T, M, compact=false) -%}
<div class="row">
  <div class="c-tk">
    {%- if r.href %}<a class="tk" href="{{ r.href }}">{{ r.ticker }}</a>{% else %}<span class="tk">{{ r.ticker }}</span>{% endif %}
    {#- `default` substitutes only for UNDEFINED, not for None, and the artifact
        ships "name_zh": null on most rows — without the boolean flag every ZH row
        printed the literal string "None" under its ticker (§10). -#}
    <span class="nm"><span class="l-en">{{ r.name | default(r.ticker, true) }}</span><span class="l-zh">{{ r.name_zh | default(r.name | default(r.ticker, true), true) }}</span></span>
  </div>
  <div class="c-gain">
    {{ figcell(r, T) }}
    <span class="cap">{{ t(M.cap_en, M.cap_zh) }}</span>
  </div>
  {%- if not compact %}<div class="c-sp">{{ spark(r.spark, r.episode_high) }}</div>{% endif %}
  <div class="c-legs">
    {#- An unreadable row renders NO wear marks at all. Three empty outlined slots
        mean "measured and clear" on this page, and that would be a lie here:
        nothing was measured, so nothing is drawn. The spark still renders — it is
        a picture of price, not a reading. -#}
    {%- if r.state == 'no_read' %}
    <span class="legs clean"{% if r.checks and r.checks.total %} data-tip-en="Only {{ r.checks.evaluated }} of the {{ r.checks.total }} checks this group makes could be made on this name, so the board does not place it in a state." data-tip-zh="本分组的 {{ r.checks.total }} 项检查中，只有 {{ r.checks.evaluated }} 项能在这只个股上完成，因此看板不给它归入任何状态。"{% endif %}>{{ t('no similar runs to compare', '没有可比的历史行情') }}</span>
    {%- else %}
    {{ wear(r.legs | length if r.legs else 0) }}
    {%- if r.legs %}
    <span class="legs">
      {%- for g in r.legs[:3] %}
      <span class="leg"{% if g.tip_en %} data-tip-en="{{ g.tip_en }}{{ prov_en(g, M) }}"{% if g.tip_zh %} data-tip-zh="{{ g.tip_zh }}{{ prov_zh(g, M) }}"{% endif %}{% endif %}><span class="l-en">{{ g.words_en }}</span><span class="l-zh">{{ g.words_zh | default(g.words_en) }}</span></span>
      {%- endfor %}
    </span>
    {%- else %}
    {#- No legs: rather than repeat one constant down 90 rows (Law 4), say the
        one thing that still varies per name and that the spark is drawing —
        how far this close sits under the run's own high. Computed from data
        already on the row, so it can never fall out of sync with the picture. -#}
    {%- set _hi = r.episode_high if r.episode_high else ((r.spark | reject('none') | list | max) if r.spark else none) -%}
    {%- set _lo = (r.spark | reject('none') | list | last) if r.spark else none -%}
    {%- set _off = ((_lo - _hi) / _hi) if (_hi and _lo and _hi > 0) else none -%}
    <span class="legs clean">
      {%- if _off is not none and _off > -0.01 -%}{{ t('sitting at its high', '正处于自身高点') }}
      {%- elif _off is not none -%}<span class="l-en">{{ '%.0f' % (_off * -100) }}% under its high</span><span class="l-zh">低于自身高点 {{ '%.0f' % (_off * -100) }}%</span>
      {%- else -%}{{ t('nothing has slipped', '暂无转弱迹象') }}{%- endif -%}
    </span>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
  <div class="c-lib">{{ analog(r.analog, T.library | default({}), M) }}</div>
</div>
{%- endmacro %}

